{"h": {"measure": "A", "k": 100, "control": "D0"}, "sp": "nb", "rep": 128, "hyps": [{"edit_edge": 3, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 5, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "higher", "why": "When edge 5 is cut, node 2's computation never reaches the output, so adding a conv on the direct 0->3 edge restores more capacity than when edge 5 already supplies a conv path."}, {"edit_edge": 3, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 3, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "higher", "why": "Replacing an empty edge with a conv adds a new path, whereas replacing an existing skip or pool on edge 3 removes a useful residual-like shortcut."}, {"edit_edge": 5, "edit_op": "none", "cond_edge": 4, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "lower", "why": "If edge 4 is already absent, removing edge 5 leaves only the shallow 0->3 edge feeding the output, which collapses accuracy far more than when 1->3 still exists."}, {"edit_edge": 0, "edit_op": "none", "cond_edge": 1, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "lower", "why": "With edge 1 absent, removing edge 0 disconnects nodes 1 and 2 from the input entirely, leaving only edge 3, a much larger loss than when 0->2 remains."}, {"edit_edge": 0, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 2, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "lower", "why": "When edge 2 is absent, node 1 only feeds the output via edge 4, so adding a conv on edge 0 contributes less depth than when it also feeds node 2."}, {"edit_edge": 3, "edit_op": "skip_connect", "cond_edge": 3, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "higher", "why": "Adding a skip on an empty input-to-output edge creates a residual shortcut that eases optimisation, while replacing a conv with skip removes capacity."}, {"edit_edge": 5, "edit_op": "skip_connect", "cond_edge": 5, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "higher", "why": "Filling an empty edge 5 with skip reconnects node 2's conv features to the output, whereas swapping out a conv or pool on edge 5 loses parameters or receptive field."}, {"edit_edge": 4, "edit_op": "skip_connect", "cond_edge": 4, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "higher", "why": "Reconnecting node 1 to the output with a skip adds an aggregation path, while replacing an existing 3x3 conv on edge 4 with skip removes learnable capacity."}, {"edit_edge": 2, "edit_op": "avg_pool_3x3", "cond_edge": 2, "cond_op": "skip_connect", "direction": "higher", "why": "Swapping a parameter-free skip for avg-pool costs little, whereas swapping a 3x3 conv for avg-pool removes a key learnable operation and hurts a lot."}, {"edit_edge": 5, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 0, "cond_op": "avg_pool_3x3", "direction": "higher", "why": "Pooling-dominated cells have almost no learnable capacity, so introducing a 3x3 conv on the final edge gives a larger gain than in cells that already contain convolutions."}], "tok": 15062, "bad": 0, "probes": [[["nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "none", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3"], [3, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "none", "nor_conv_3x3", "none"], [3, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "none", "nor_conv_3x3", "skip_connect"], [3, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "skip_connect", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3"], [3, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "skip_connect", "nor_conv_3x3", "none"], [3, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "avg_pool_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3"], [3, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "avg_pool_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "none"], [3, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["nor_conv_1x1", "skip_connect", "nor_conv_1x1", "none", "skip_connect", "nor_conv_1x1"], [3, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["nor_conv_1x1", "skip_connect", "nor_conv_1x1", "none", "skip_connect", "none"], [3, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["none", "none", "none", "none", "none", "nor_conv_3x3"], [3, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["none", "nor_conv_3x3", "none", "none", "none", "nor_conv_3x3"], [3, "nor